{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"The RUO NovaSeq 6000 control software has shipped one release in about 35 months, against five or six for the NovaSeq X over a similar span.","detail":"The 6000 downloads page lists v1.8.0 (Jul 21, 2022), v1.8.1 (Nov 6, 2023) and v1.8.2 (Aug 25, 2025). That is a 21-month gap between the last two, and no release in the 13.6 months from 25 Aug 2025 to 12 Oct 2026. The X Series notes list v1.1.0 (27 Jun 2023), v1.2.0 (2 Nov 2023), v1.2.2 (13 May 2024), v1.3.0 (2 Dec 2024), v1.3.1 (23 Jun 2025) and v1.4.0 (28 Jul 2026 on the EMEA page; the PDF says March 2026). X intervals are about 6.4, 6.6 and 6.7 months, then 9 to 13 months. Since Nov 2023 the 6000 has had 1 release and the X has had 4 to 5.","url":"https://support.illumina.com/sequencing/sequencing_instruments/novaseq-6000/downloads.html","date":"2026-10-12","source_name":"Illumina support: NovaSeq 6000 downloads; X Series documentation (EMEA)","source_type":"archive","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"This gives a dated, quantified 6000 vs X software cadence. The known list had only a thin 'v1.8.2 Aug 2025' mention."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"The 6000's Clarity LIMS integration has had only security-patch releases in 2026, while the X integration got new features.","detail":"6000 API v3.7.0 (Jul 2024) moved properties into the database. v3.7.1 (Apr 2026) fixed security vulnerabilities and an error-log retry. v3.7.2 (Jun 2026, document version 5) lists no features, only 'Fixed security vulnerabilities'. The X Series v1.4.0 integration (Apr 2026) added 5B flow-cell support, 1.5B with the 600-cycle kit, and a new v2.0 sequencing workflow. The 6000 integration has therefore had no feature in about 27 months (Jul 2024 to Oct 2026), and the X integration gained new flow cells in 2026.","url":"https://help.connected.illumina.com/clarity-lims/instruments-and-integrations/novaseq6k-api/novaseq-6000-api-based-v3.7.2/novaseq6k-api-v3.7.2-release-notes.md","date":"2026-06","source_name":"Illumina Clarity LIMS help: NovaSeq6k API v3.7.x and NovaSeq X v1.4.0 release notes","source_type":"archive","quote":"Fixed security vulnerabilities.","strength":"medium","why_new":"Not in the known list. The 2026 LIMS patch history shows maintenance-only mode for the 6000 against active X development."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"New product features and flow cells are being built for the X only. The 5B flow cell and 1.5B-600-cycle support came to the X in 2026, with no equivalent on the 6000.","detail":"X Control Software v1.4.0 (RTA 4.29.3 to 4.50.12) added the 5B flow cell for 100, 200 and 300 cycles, index autodetection and an alternate laser engine for uptime. The 6000 v1.8.2 page lists no new kit support. The only 6000 compatibility note is that v1.5 reagent kits need v1.7 or later, an old requirement. The mid-range 5B tier is the one that competes with AVITI and NextSeq, and it is X-only.","url":"https://www.illumina.com/science/genomics-research/articles/novaseq-x-software-update-v1-4-improves-data-quality-and-custome.html","date":"2026-03","source_name":"Illumina science article and release notes 200079828","source_type":"press","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"Known items mention the 5B only as a price tier. This ties it to X-only software investment."},
